# CachyOS. Assembled 2026-08-17 from CachyOS's own branding script, which is what produces the file on
# an installed machine: https://github.com/CachyOS/cachyos-hooks (cachyos-branding, update_os_release),
# packaged as cachyos-hooks 2026.02.05 at https://github.com/CachyOS/CachyOS-PKGBUILDS/tree/master/cachyos-hooks
# The hook triggers on the filesystem package and seds Arch's file
# (https://gitlab.archlinux.org/archlinux/packaging/packages/filesystem/-/raw/main/os-release) in
# place, so there is no packaged file to copy. Every line below except PRIVACY_POLICY_URL is
# corroborated verbatim by pastes of real machines on CachyOS's own forum,
# https://discuss.cachyos.org/t/helldivers-2-hangs-in-language-selection/23489 for the identity fields
# and https://discuss.cachyos.org/t/va-api-hardware-acceleration-is-not-working-cachyos-intel-celeron-n4500/16783
# for the URLs; PRIVACY_POLICY_URL is Arch's, kept because the script never edits that line.
#
# Two things this fixture cannot show. ID_LIKE only became reliable on 2025-11-14, when an inverted
# condition in the "add ID_LIKE when missing" branch was fixed, so an install whose filesystem package
# has not been upgraded since then has ID=cachyos and no ID_LIKE at all. And the live ISO ships a
# static file with ID=arch and no ID_LIKE. In both of those states Ansible's own answer is Archlinux
# anyway, through /etc/arch-release, which the derivation takes before it ever looks at ID_LIKE.
NAME="CachyOS Linux"
PRETTY_NAME="CachyOS"
ID=cachyos
ID_LIKE=arch
BUILD_ID=rolling
ANSI_COLOR="38;2;23;147;209"
HOME_URL="https://cachyos.org/"
DOCUMENTATION_URL="https://wiki.cachyos.org/"
SUPPORT_URL="https://discuss.cachyos.org/"
BUG_REPORT_URL="https://github.com/cachyos"
PRIVACY_POLICY_URL="https://terms.archlinux.org/docs/privacy-policy/"
LOGO=cachyos
